WEBVTT

01:24.910 --> 01:27.080
<i>Small aircraft detected.</i>

01:27.920 --> 01:30.090
<i>Mutant signals present.</i>

01:31.090 --> 01:33.550
<i>It's the X-Men's Blackbird.</i>

01:35.590 --> 01:38.090
<i>It's headed this way.</i>

01:39.180 --> 01:40.390
The X-Men...

01:41.180 --> 01:43.140
so they're finally coming.

01:44.560 --> 01:48.190
Activate our counter-measures.

01:53.230 --> 01:59.700
<b><i>U-MEN - Mutant Hunt</i></b>

01:57.910 --> 02:00.030
We're entering Tohoku airspace.

02:00.030 --> 02:01.370
I'm lowering our altitude.

02:02.240 --> 02:06.710
We should reach the lchiki estate
in thirty minutes.

02:06.710 --> 02:07.710
Understood.

02:10.630 --> 02:14.050
That the upgraded portable Cerebro?

02:14.050 --> 02:14.920
Yes.

02:14.920 --> 02:18.090
It can now detect mutants
without the aid of a telepath.

02:18.550 --> 02:21.260
Since you checked it
as soon as we got here,

02:21.260 --> 02:24.850
I bet you think that Chuck's powers
are getting weaker too, right?

02:25.430 --> 02:28.730
I'm just trying to be thorough.

02:28.730 --> 02:29.980
Yeah, alright.

02:45.580 --> 02:47.960
So they've come...

02:47.960 --> 02:49.370
<i>Don't worry.</i>

02:49.370 --> 02:54.170
<i>With our technology,
we have nothing to fear from the X-Men.</i>

02:54.840 --> 02:57.050
Sounds delightful.

02:57.050 --> 02:58.090
<i>If you'll excuse me...</i>

03:03.220 --> 03:04.810
Professor X...

03:05.260 --> 03:08.560
you'll be the next
to come visit, won't you?

03:28.330 --> 03:28.910
Yes...

03:29.580 --> 03:33.250
when we looked for her with our neighbors,
we found Hisako's bag right here...

03:33.960 --> 03:37.920
If I had picked her up at the bus stop,
maybe this wouldn't have...

03:38.460 --> 03:42.640
On the day it happened,
our car wasn't starting...

03:42.640 --> 03:45.350
But she said there was
a test she couldn't miss,

03:45.350 --> 03:47.180
so she took the bus instead.

03:47.680 --> 03:51.310
The other students were
with her when she left school,

03:51.310 --> 03:53.810
but between the bus stop
and our home,

03:53.810 --> 03:55.230
she would've been all alone...

03:55.610 --> 03:57.020
And this is where...

04:00.740 --> 04:04.070
You normally drive her
to school, then?

04:04.070 --> 04:04.910
Yes.

04:05.490 --> 04:07.540
Because other children
have gone missing,

04:07.540 --> 04:09.750
or been spirited away...

04:11.330 --> 04:12.250
There were others?

04:20.050 --> 04:21.380
Over the last few years,

04:21.380 --> 04:27.100
over twenty young mutants have been
reported missing around here.

04:27.100 --> 04:30.390
But the real number
is actually higher...

04:30.390 --> 04:32.480
There are many
who don't want to publicize

04:32.480 --> 04:35.610
that so many children
have gone missing, so...

04:35.980 --> 04:37.980
Why would they want
to keep it a secret?

04:38.400 --> 04:42.320
There's been a lot of
strange phenomena and accidents lately,

04:42.320 --> 04:46.370
and some people have been saying
that mutants were to blame...

04:47.070 --> 04:49.540
People were afraid of
being suspected,

04:49.540 --> 04:51.540
or being persecuted...

04:53.000 --> 04:58.290
ls there ever going to be a time when
people understand mutants?

05:12.020 --> 05:15.440
The number of people who have gone
missing is really troubling...

05:16.310 --> 05:18.820
it really is mutant hunting...

05:19.860 --> 05:21.480
If that's the case,

05:21.480 --> 05:23.530
I'd put money on it
being the U-Men.

05:24.110 --> 05:28.530
I've heard rumors that they've been
hiding out in Japan lately.

05:29.370 --> 05:30.280
U-Men?

05:30.740 --> 05:33.250
They're a group of mad scientists

05:33.250 --> 05:38.420
who want to use mutant powers
to exterminate humanity.

05:40.800 --> 05:43.380
That was from
Mr. Fujiwara's grandfather!

05:43.380 --> 05:45.970
His grandson has gone missing!

05:47.090 --> 05:48.260
Honey!

05:50.680 --> 05:54.640
He went to make a delivery
yesterday for his job,

05:54.640 --> 05:56.440
and has been missing
since then...

05:57.400 --> 05:58.810
Is this boy?

06:00.520 --> 06:01.860
He's a mutant.

06:09.870 --> 06:11.370
We'll check out where he works.

06:12.200 --> 06:14.250
You two head to
the Fujiwara's house.

06:14.250 --> 06:15.040
Right.

06:15.040 --> 06:16.250
We'll meet up later.

06:25.840 --> 06:28.340
Let's see...

06:28.720 --> 06:29.430
Uh...

06:29.430 --> 06:30.640
yeah, that's him.

06:31.180 --> 06:32.430
And you're sure?

06:32.430 --> 06:36.730
Yeah, but it wasn't yesterday,
he's been gone for two weeks now.

06:37.640 --> 06:41.900
See that restaurant up
on the mountain?

06:43.070 --> 06:47.070
I got word that he made the delivery,
but ain't heard from him since...

06:49.570 --> 06:53.280
...I found out about this later,
but it turns out he's a mutie.

06:53.280 --> 06:55.240
What's he gotten into, anyway?

06:57.830 --> 06:59.830
Those freaks are always
using their powers

06:59.830 --> 07:03.170
to cause accidents and mess
with normal folks, after all.

07:03.710 --> 07:06.880
Wait, don't tell me
you two are?

07:06.880 --> 07:08.670
Got a problem with that, bub?

07:09.260 --> 07:10.300
Give it a rest, Wolverine.

07:10.640 --> 07:13.390
Uh, well, I didn't really mean, uh...

07:14.100 --> 07:17.980
Oh, I've got a delivery
to make, so

07:19.520 --> 07:20.480
Sorry to bother you.

07:25.650 --> 07:30.860
Jeez, what are a bunch of them
doing around here?

07:51.050 --> 07:56.390
<i>Has anything we've done for
mutantkind made any difference?</i>

08:01.020 --> 08:03.730
<i>What did Jean die for?</i>

08:19.290 --> 08:21.290
A restaurant in the mountains?

08:22.580 --> 08:24.170
<i>That high school kid apparently
made a delivery</i>

08:24.170 --> 08:26.130
<i>right before he went missing.</i>

08:27.500 --> 08:28.800
We're heading there now.

08:28.800 --> 08:29.710
<i>Scott!</i>

08:30.460 --> 08:33.840
The Fujiwara's grandfather family
didn't call the lchikis.

08:33.840 --> 08:34.590
<i>What!?</i>

08:34.590 --> 08:36.050
They were trying to
maintain appearances,

08:36.050 --> 08:38.260
and hadn't discussed
the disappearance with anyone.

08:39.930 --> 08:42.390
Including the lchiki family.

08:50.190 --> 08:53.320
That call was just bait
to lure us into a trap!

08:53.820 --> 08:55.740
Sounds good to me!

08:56.820 --> 08:58.330
And here they come!

09:11.800 --> 09:15.180
I guess the U-Men've
finally got their act together.

09:15.590 --> 09:17.720
How can you be
so sure it's them?

09:19.260 --> 09:21.640
I fought one of
their old robots before.

09:23.060 --> 09:26.350
This new model makes that old piece of
junk look downright cute and cuddly.

09:29.610 --> 09:31.280
Get to work, Cyclops!

09:32.190 --> 09:33.070
Got it!

10:07.850 --> 10:09.360
X-Men...

10:24.620 --> 10:26.790
I'm worried about
Scott and Logan.

10:31.290 --> 10:33.880
Let's worry about
ourselves for now.

10:33.880 --> 10:34.710
Right.

11:29.060 --> 11:30.690
Are you alright, Storm!?

11:31.770 --> 11:33.360
Yes, somewhat...

11:59.220 --> 12:00.130
Cyclops!

12:00.840 --> 12:02.180
Quit rushing straight at 'em!

12:02.180 --> 12:03.180
You're gonna get wiped out!

12:03.640 --> 12:04.640
<i>Because of them...</i>

12:07.140 --> 12:08.140
<i>Because of them!</i>

12:15.900 --> 12:18.110
<i>Because of people like them,</i>

12:18.110 --> 12:20.650
<i>there's always going to be
unprovoked attacks on mutants!</i>

12:35.420 --> 12:37.460
You think rushing at 'em like
a rookie's gonna help!?

12:37.460 --> 12:38.800
Get it together!

12:38.800 --> 12:39.710
Here they come!

13:12.620 --> 13:15.420
Looks like we're
wrapped up here, Cyclops.

13:17.460 --> 13:18.710
I know how you feel, bub...

13:19.340 --> 13:21.880
But if I'm the calm one in this tag-team,
something is really wrong.

13:21.880 --> 13:22.970
You need to pull it together.

13:23.550 --> 13:24.970
Mind your own business.

13:27.930 --> 13:28.640
Let's move.

13:30.560 --> 13:32.810
<i>The mobilized force
has been eliminated.</i>

13:32.810 --> 13:33.730
It's fine...

13:33.730 --> 13:35.600
this was expected.

13:35.600 --> 13:37.730
We were able to gather
the data we needed.

13:37.730 --> 13:41.570
Let's get to work on analyzing

13:41.570 --> 13:44.990
the X-Men's powers and designing
a new batch of counter-measures.

13:44.990 --> 13:46.610
Leave it to me.

13:48.530 --> 13:53.000
They will cower in
the face of our science...

13:57.420 --> 13:58.130
What I?

13:58.710 --> 13:59.920
The U-Men?

13:59.920 --> 14:01.500
<i>Logan was able to confirm it</i>

14:01.500 --> 14:03.380
<i>after examining one of
their downed robots.</i>

14:03.380 --> 14:07.130
<i>The lack of new mutant signatures,
Hisako lchiki going missing,</i>

14:07.130 --> 14:11.010
<i>and the string of other mutant
disappearances around here...</i>

14:11.010 --> 14:13.930
<i>It seems like they're at
the root of it.</i>

14:13.930 --> 14:16.730
The U-Men are a group of
<i>homo</i> sapiens

14:16.730 --> 14:18.980
supremacists who try to
harvest mutant organs

14:18.980 --> 14:24.530
as a means of being able to fight
on even footing against our powers.

14:25.490 --> 14:26.990
<i>It sounds like them.</i>

14:28.030 --> 14:30.410
We're going to meet up
with Scott and head toward

14:30.410 --> 14:32.330
what we believe is their base.

14:33.240 --> 14:35.830
Be very careful.

14:40.830 --> 14:43.590
This battle will be
very difficult...

15:00.230 --> 15:02.060
<i>The Sasaki Institute is closed.</i>

15:03.020 --> 15:04.480
<i>No reason is listed.</i>

15:13.410 --> 15:15.120
This place used to be a hospital?

15:15.120 --> 15:15.660
Yes...

15:16.410 --> 15:18.370
A special medical research group
was using it.

15:19.870 --> 15:22.460
It was closed twenty years ago,

15:22.460 --> 15:26.340
and the local people are
afraid to even come near...

15:29.050 --> 15:33.430
Sounds like the perfect place
for a bunch of rats to hide.

15:39.230 --> 15:40.850
There's no sign of anyone...

15:40.850 --> 15:41.940
Be on guard.

15:41.940 --> 15:43.270
It could be a trap.

15:43.270 --> 15:44.940
Sounds like fun to me...

15:46.780 --> 15:47.570
What is that?

15:53.120 --> 15:54.120
It...

15:54.120 --> 15:56.080
it hurts...

15:58.290 --> 16:00.160
H-help me...

16:00.790 --> 16:02.580
H-help me...

16:03.710 --> 16:04.380
It...

16:04.380 --> 16:07.210
It hurts!

16:09.420 --> 16:11.630
That's the boy who went missing
from his job!

16:12.180 --> 16:13.800
Wait, Cyclops!

16:40.580 --> 16:41.830
Cyclops!

16:42.620 --> 16:44.000
What the hell was that!?

16:44.000 --> 16:45.170
Get your head in the game!

16:49.090 --> 16:50.550
Wolverine, don't!

16:50.550 --> 16:52.010
He's a kidnapped mutant!

16:52.220 --> 16:54.800
But if he's been changed
this much!

17:00.850 --> 17:03.770
The scanner's confirmed that
his biology's been warped beyond

17:03.770 --> 17:05.400
any chance of restoration.

17:05.730 --> 17:09.230
It pains me to say it,
but there's no way to turn him back.

17:09.230 --> 17:10.780
He can't be saved.

17:10.780 --> 17:12.110
But still...

17:12.900 --> 17:13.650
Cyclops!

17:26.000 --> 17:27.540
What's happened is a tragedy,

17:27.540 --> 17:29.800
but the only thing
we can do for him now

17:29.800 --> 17:31.630
is release him from his suffering!

17:36.340 --> 17:36.890
Storm!

17:49.230 --> 17:49.980
Stop!

17:49.980 --> 17:50.730
Don't do this!

17:51.070 --> 17:52.070
Snap out of it!

17:58.620 --> 18:00.080
Now, Cyclops!

18:02.790 --> 18:04.410
Cyclops!

18:10.210 --> 18:11.670
Cyclops!

18:54.630 --> 18:56.420
It doesn't hurt anymore...

18:57.170 --> 18:58.380
Thank you...

19:03.970 --> 19:05.390
Save...

19:05.390 --> 19:06.350
them...

19:06.810 --> 19:07.890
there are...

19:07.890 --> 19:09.190
more...

19:09.690 --> 19:13.860
inside...

19:21.950 --> 19:25.330
What could the U-Men be planning?

19:26.370 --> 19:28.080
What's the point of this?

19:28.080 --> 19:32.790
We just killed an innocent mutant!

19:42.640 --> 19:46.060
You gonna let Jean die
for nothing, you bastard!?

19:46.470 --> 19:49.770
How can't you understand!?

19:50.600 --> 19:53.190
Your feelings aren't
what's important!

19:53.650 --> 19:55.770
Being an X-Man means
you've got a duty!

19:56.150 --> 19:57.980
And that goes double when
you're the damn leader!

20:15.840 --> 20:16.800
Come on.

20:23.220 --> 20:24.800
Let's get a move on.

20:26.050 --> 20:28.100
Storm, are you alright?

20:28.100 --> 20:28.640
Yes...

20:44.450 --> 20:46.870
What the hell is this place?

20:47.580 --> 20:50.200
Some kind of laboratory,
I'd imagine.

20:56.960 --> 20:58.250
This girl...

21:01.260 --> 21:02.840
It's Hisako lchiki!

21:02.840 --> 21:03.840
What!?

21:06.180 --> 21:08.850
There's a woman here too.

21:17.150 --> 21:17.730
Why...

21:18.480 --> 21:19.230
<i>why!?</i>

21:21.230 --> 21:22.320
<i>Why is she here!?</i>

23:03.250 --> 23:06.460
A mutant telepath named Emma
is found being held captive by the U-Men,

23:06.460 --> 23:07.970
along with Hisako.

23:08.800 --> 23:12.890
The X-Men are suspicious when
she claims that she was Hisako's teacher,

23:12.890 --> 23:14.760
and had tried to rescue her.

23:15.430 --> 23:19.560
And one of the U-Men's mad scientists,
Todd attacks.

23:20.350 --> 23:22.360
During the intense battle,

23:22.360 --> 23:24.770
Hisako's mutant powers activate...

23:25.980 --> 23:31.160
<b><i>Armor - Awakening</i></b>

23:26.230 --> 23:27.820
Next time on X-Men...

23:28.550 --> 23:29.440
Awakening
